<BaseLayout
  title="About · Ish Rastogi"
  description="Ish Rastogi: engineer, home cook and enthusiastic wanderer, writing about .NET, cloud and AI."
>
  <h1>About</h1>

  <p>
    Hi, I'm Ish. By day I'm a Technical Lead who has spent 18 years building
    software in C# and .NET. Off the keyboard, you'll usually find me in the
    kitchen or out exploring somewhere new.
  </p>

  <h2>The day job</h2>
  <p>
    I design and build distributed systems for UK insurance: the kind of
    platforms that quietly handle millions of requests a day. I've led a large
    move to Kubernetes on AWS, and these days most of my energy goes into AI
    engineering: building agents in .NET and figuring out how to make them
    reliable enough for real production systems.
  </p>
  <p>
    This blog is where I write up what I learn along the way, including the
    things that didn't work.
  </p>

  <h2>In the kitchen</h2>
  <p>
    Cooking is how I switch off. I love experimenting with paneer curries, and
    my current favourite to make is thread paneer. It turns out cooking and
    engineering aren't that different: you follow the recipe until you
    understand it well enough to break the rules.
  </p>

  <h2>Out and about</h2>
  <p>
    I'm happiest wandering somewhere I haven't been before: a new city, a
    coastal path or just a different corner of Norwich. Some of my
    favourite places so far are Switzerland, Iceland and Wales. Next on my list is
    Kedarnath, India.
  </p>

  <h2>Say hello</h2>
  <p>
    Whether it's .NET, AI, a recipe recommendation or a place I should visit,
    I'd love to hear from you. Find me on
    <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/your-profile">LinkedIn</a> or
    <a href="https://github.com/ishnetcode">GitHub</a>.
  </p>
